I buy things all the time--my current character just levelported up
from Orcustown to escape a purple L, and bought some things as he
wandered back to his stash.  And he's certainly not to the point where
funds are infinite; I carefully measured how much I could spend and
still afford as many clairvoyance purchases as I calculated I'd want to
finish mapping Gehennom.

Getting a pet after minetown is easy, but I often find it preferrable
to avoid it (esp. if I lack a magic lamp)--otherwise ranged attacks
will eventually result in an angry god.  Obviously there are some
exceptions (even my non-pacifist healers will often play pet support
games).  I'll even ditch the pet soon after minetown/sokoban if I know
I'm going to be throwing a lot of magic missiles (or other ricocheting
effects) around.



